  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DevFlow",
      "text": "**Version `1.5.1`** · 2026-10-11\n\nA **multi-agent workflow orchestration plugin for [DeepSeek Harness (dsh)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)**.\n\nDevFlow turns a dsh session into a small delivery organisation with a visible control plane:"
    },
    {
      "section": "DevFlow",
      "text": "- **Roles** — a Commander (总指挥) that plans and dispatches, fixed employees (architect / backend / frontend / code-auditor), and temporary sub-agents created per task.\n- **State machine** — dispatch → execution → audit → rework → acceptance. Every step is a persisted business entity under `<workspace>/.devflow`, with an append-only journal.\n- **Dispatch plane** — `devflow_*` tools (task / scope / assignment / dispatch / transition / roster), concurrency-capped at 5 with queueing, and a dispatch diagnostic for every hand-off.\n- **Visual panel** — a canvas with one edge per dispatch, a roster bar (`fixed / temporary`, live `concurrency N/5`), and a per-node inspector, mounted in the dsh right sidebar."
    },
    {
      "section": "DevFlow",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "| | |\n|---|---|\n| Node | `^22.19.0` or `>=24` |\n| pnpm | any recent version |\n| dsh | installed, with a profile you can edit (e.g. `~/.dsh/profiles/web`) · target range `>=0.1.7-rc.1 <0.3.0` (**dsh 0.1.5 is no longer supported**) |\n| OS | Windows is the tested platform (the preset wires `tool-pwsh` on win32 / `tool-bash` elsewhere) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install (one command)",
      "text": "**Windows (PowerShell)** — copy this single line:\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/BinXie-lixiangdehua/dsh-devflow.git \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.dsh\\local-plugins\\dsh-devflow\"; & \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.dsh\\local-plugins\\dsh-devflow\\install.cmd\"\n```\n\nOr, if you already have the folder, `install.cmd` on its own (double-clickable — it just calls `install.ps1`).\n\nUseful switches:\n\n```powershell"
    },
    {
      "section": "see what would change, touch nothing",
      "text": ".\\install.ps1 -DryRun"
    },
    {
      "section": "install into a different dsh home / profile, or skip the preset step",
      "text": ".\\install.ps1 -DshHome 'C:\\Users\\me\\.dsh' -Profile 'web'\n.\\install.ps1 -SkipPreset"
    },
    {
      "section": "install a specific tag/branch",
      "text": ".\\install.ps1 -Ref 'v1.5.1'\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "What the installer actually changes",
      "text": "1. **Puts the plugin on disk** — clones (or copies) into `~/.dsh/local-plugins/dsh-devflow` by default.\n2. **Installs the plugin's own dependencies** — runs `pnpm install` **inside the plugin directory**. `lib/index.js` is ESM and every `@deepseek-ai/*` package is a peer dependency, so installing only the *profile* leaves them unresolvable and the host fails to import the plugin (`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: Cannot find package '@deepseek-ai/cordis'`) while older hosts report only a bare `failed to import`. This step runs **before** the profile is touched: a bad install fails loudly here instead of leaving a rewritten profile behind. Pass `-SkipPluginDeps` to skip it deliberately.\n3. **Registers the profile bundle** — in `~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/package.json`:\n   adds `\"@xiaoxie-ide/dsh-devflow\": \"link:<install-dir>\"` to `dependencies` and the package name to `dsh.profile.bundles`.\n   The original file is saved as `package.json.bak-devflow-<timestamp>`.\n4. **Links dependencies** — runs `pnpm install` inside the profile so the `link:` symlink really exists.\n5. **Deploys the agent preset — both forms, because the two dsh generations read different ones** —\n   * **legacy (dsh `0.1.5`)**: "
    },
    {
      "section": "What the installer actually changes",
      "text": "The target version is decided by **detection, in this order**: `-DshVersion` → **the running dsh host** (its process working directory is read; no admin rights, no unsigned binaries — filtered by `DSH_HOME`) → the `dsh` command on `PATH` → the profile's `@deepseek-ai/dsh` symlink. It always prints the **detection source path** and warns when the profile's symlink and the running host disagree; `-PresetDeclaration on|off` overrides."
    },
    {
      "section": "What the installer actually changes",
      "text": "`-DryRun` writes **nothing** (it reports which files it would touch).\n\nThen **restart dsh**, open a session, and pick the **DevFlow** preset. That is the whole install.\n\n> Why the `?rev=` token: a standing mount re-imports a row only when its stamp changes, and an unchanged URL is served from the ESM module cache. Bumping `rev` after a rebuild is what lets the running host pick up a new `lib/` without a restart."
    },
    {
      "section": "Manual install",
      "text": "If you prefer doing it by hand:\n\n```powershell"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. get the code where you want it",
      "text": "git clone https://github.com/BinXie-lixiangdehua/dsh-devflow.git D:\\plugins\\dsh-devflow"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. materialise the link",
      "text": "pnpm install --dir \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.dsh\\profiles\\web\""
    },
    {
      "section": "with:                         'file:///D:/plugins/dsh-devflow/lib/host/preset-activation.js?rev=local'",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build from source",
      "text": "`lib/` is committed on purpose so that installing needs no toolchain. If you change `src/`, rebuild and re-commit the artefacts:\n\n```bash\npnpm install\npnpm typecheck   # tsc, both projects\npnpm build       # tsc + tsdown  ->  lib/index.js, lib/client.js\npnpm check       # node --check on both bundles\n\nGate order matters: `typecheck → build → check → test` (`check` inspects `lib/`, so running it before `build` checks a stale bundle)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build from source",
      "text": "After a rebuild, bump the `?rev=` token in the deployed preset, or restart dsh, to make the host load the new module."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "1. Remove `~/.dsh/.agent-presets/devflow/`.\n2. Undo step 2 above: drop the dependency line and the `dsh.profile.bundles` entry (or restore `package.json.bak-devflow-<timestamp>`).\n3. `pnpm install` in the profile again, then delete the plugin folder.\n\n`.devflow` directories live **inside your project workspaces**, not in this repository. They are your project state — remove them yourself if you want a clean slate."
    },
    {
      "section": "Layout",
      "text": "```\nsrc/host/          plugin host plane: tools, state machine, storage, journal, guards\nsrc/client/        the panel: canvas, projection, roster, sidebar slot\npresets/devflow/   the dsh agent preset (activation row + capability rows)\ntests/             vitest suites (unit + guard/isolation)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Versioning",
      "text": "Releases follow semver. Every published snapshot gets an annotated tag (`v1.1.0`, `v1.1.1`, …) and the `version` field in `package.json` matches that tag, so `git checkout v1.1.0` and a pinned install both mean the same thing."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE)."
    }
  ],
